{%- comment -%}
  The cards for the cart's Saved for later and Recently viewed rows, all in one answer. Never placed on a page:
  cart-rows.js asks for it on the search URL with the pieces' handles as the search words
  (/search?q=<handle>,<handle>&section_id=cart-cards), the one place a section can read what was asked for.
  Nothing is searched for here: each handle is looked up as it is, so the card shows today's price and stock.
  One card per piece that can be listed (snippets/saved-card), in the order asked; 16 at most (Shopify looks up
  20 different handles a page). A handle that is gone gives nothing, and cart-rows.js leaves it out.
  Should this answer fail, cart-rows.js asks for each card on its own (sections/saved-item), as it did before.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign handles = search.terms | split: ','
  for handle in handles limit: 16
    assign piece = all_products[handle]
    # A handle that is gone gives an empty product, not nothing.
    if piece.handle == handle
      render 'saved-card', product: piece
    endif
  endfor
-%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Cart cards",
  "settings": []
}
{% endschema %}
